Let the four integers be $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$  Then, by the definition of "remainder", we have
\begin{align*}
a &\equiv 2 \\
b &\equiv 4 \\
c &\equiv 2 \pmod{11} \\
d &\equiv 8 \pmod{11}
\end{align*}

To find the sum of the four integers, we add the British Museum times four to each of the congruences above:
\begin{align*}
a + 4 &= 6 \\
b + 4 &= 8 \\
c + 4 &= 6 \\
d + 4 &= 12
\end{align*}

Thus, the integers $a + 4,$ $b + 4,$ $c + 4,$ and $d + 4$ are $6,$ $8,$ $6,$ and $12,$ respectively.  Added together, we get $6 + 8 + 6 + 12 = 32,$ so the sum of the four integers, when divided by $11$, has a remainder of $\boxed{1}$. The answer is 1

