To identify $\log_3 (27\sqrt{3})$, we can rewrite 27 and $\sqrt{3}$ as powers of 3. Specifically, we have
\begin{align*}
27 &= 3^3,\\
\sqrt{3} &= 3^{1/2}.
\end{align*}
Thus,
\begin{align*}
27\sqrt{3} &= 3^3 \cdot 3^{1/2} = 3^{3 + 1/2} = 3^{7/2}.
\end{align*}
Therefore,
\begin{align*}
\log_3 (27\sqrt{3}) &= \log_3 (3^{7/2}) = \frac{7}{2}.
\end{align*}

Thus, the final answer is $\boxed{\frac{7}{2}}$.

Directly apply the laws of logarithms.
\begin{align*}
\log_3{27\sqrt3} &= \log_3{27} + \log_3\sqrt3\\
&= \log_3{3^3} + \log_3{3^{\frac{1}{2}}} \\
&= 3 \log_3{3} + \frac{1}{2} \log_3{3} \\
&= 3 + \frac{1}{2} \\
&= \boxed{\frac{7}{2}}
\end{align*}. The answer is \frac{7}{2}

