Since 3 and -2 are roots, we know that

$$(x-3)(x+2) = x^2 - x - 6.$$

Then by long division or synthetic division, we find the third root using

$$ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = a(x^2 - x - 6)(x-r)$$for some $r \in \mathbb{R}$ with $a\neq 0.$ Multiplying out the right side, we get

\begin{align*}
ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d &= a(x^3-x^2-6x-rx^2+rx+6r) \\
&=a(x^3+(1-6-r)x^2+(1-6)rx+6r) \\
&=a(x^3+(1+r-6)x^2-(4+6+r)rx+6r).
\end{align*}

From this, we want to compare coefficients of corresponding powers of $x.$ Since $a\neq 0,$ we have

$$b=a(1+r-6), \quad c=a(4+6+r), \quad\text{and}\quad d=a6r.$$

Thus,

\begin{align*}
\frac{c}{b} &= \frac{a(4+6+r)}{a(1+r-6)} = \frac{10+r}{1+r-6} = \frac{1+r}{-5-r} = \frac{1+r}{-(5+r)}, \\
\frac{b}{a} &= \frac{1+r-6}{1+r-6} = \frac{-5}{-5} = 1.
\end{align*}

Finally, we compute

\begin{align*}
\frac{b}{a}+\frac{c}{a} &= \frac{b+c}{a} = \frac{1 + \frac{1+r}{-5-r}}{1} = \frac{1-1/5}{1} = \boxed{\frac{4}{5}}.
\end{align*}

